# Global store slices

Every `*.slice.ts` under `packages/sdk/src/store/global` must `extend GlobalStoreSlice` (`packages/sdk/src/store/global/global-store.slice.ts`). Nested slices may also `implement` a view interface (`DialogUIState`, `ThreadUIState`).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — standalone class, makeAutoObservable
export class ThreadSlice implements ThreadUIState {
  constructor(ctx: ThreadSliceContext) {
    this.ctx = ctx;
    makeAutoObservable(this);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD
export class ThreadSlice extends GlobalStoreSlice implements ThreadUIState {
  constructor(ctx: ThreadSliceContext, snapshot?: ThreadUISnapshot) {
    super();
    this.ctx = ctx;
    this.applySnapshot(snapshot);
    this.observe({ ctx: false, getMessageList: false });
  }

  toJS(): Record<string, unknown> {
    return this.toSnapshot();
  }

  hydrateFromSnapshot(snapshot: Record<string, unknown> | undefined) {
    this.applySnapshot(snapshot as ThreadUISnapshot | undefined);
  }
}
```

- Do **not** call `makeAutoObservable` — MobX forbids it on subclasses. Call `this.observe()` at the **end** of the constructor (pass `false` for untracked fields).
- Implement `toJS` / `hydrateFromSnapshot`. Dialog/thread persist units may keep `toSnapshot` / `fromSnapshot` and delegate.
